{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 05:34:53 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Tool call: query_entries | format_requested=readable; response_data={\"entries\": [{\"agent\": \"Codex\", \"emoji\": \"\\u2139\\ufe0f\", \"message\": \"Implemented session-scoped project storage and project-resolution guardrails (session_projects in state, set_project writes session, resolve_logging_context prefers session + blocks sentinel fallback).\", \"meta\": {\"enforce sentinel hard-fail\": \"\", \"files_changed\": \"[\\\"state/manager.py\\\", \\\"tools/set_project.py\\\", \\\"shared/logging_utils.py\\\"]\", \"log_type\": \"progress\", \"phase\": \"implementation\", \"prefer session before global fallback\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"Phase 3 requires session-scoped project resolution and current_project quarantine without renaming\\\"}\": \"\", \"reasoning\": \"{\\\"how\\\": \\\"added session_projects to state, passed session_id in set_project, and updated resolve_logging_context to use session_id and block sentinel fallback\\\", \\\"what\\\": \\\"constraints: keep current_project\"}, \"project\": \"scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"raw_line\": \"[\\u2139\\ufe0f] [2026-01-02 05:11:31 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Implemented session-scoped project storage and project-resolution guardrails (session_projects in state, set_project writes session, resolve_logging_context prefers session + blocks sentinel fallback).   files_changed=[\\\"state/manager.py\\\", \\\"tools/set_project.py\\\", \\\"shared/logging_utils.py\\\"]; phase=implementation; reasoning={\\\"how\\\": \\\"added session_projects to state, passed session_id in set_project, and updated resolve_logging_context to use session_id and block sentinel fallback\\\", \\\"what\\\": \\\"constraints: keep current_project; enforce sentinel hard-fail; prefer session before global fallback\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"Phase 3 requires session-scoped project resolution and current_project quarantine without renaming\\\"}; log_type=progress\", \"ts\": \"2026-01-02 05:11:31 UTC\"}, {\"agent\": \"Codex\", \"emoji\": \"\\u26a0\\ufe0f\", \"message\": \"Audited execution context failures and patched server tool dispatcher to normalize missing context fields (repo_root/mode/intent/affected_dev_projects) before building ExecutionContext; change in server.py to unblock MCP tool calls when client omits context payload. reasoning: {\\\"why\\\":\\\"Scribe MCP calls were failing with missing ExecutionContext; needed to restore tool operability and root-cause mismatch with client payloads.\\\",\\\"what\\\":\\\"Constraints: avoid bypass hacks, keep strict ExecutionContext validation, accept missing client context by normalizing defaults; preserve sentinel/project tool gating.\\\",\\\"how\\\":\\\"Inspected server/tool context flow, edited server.py _call_tool to fill defaults from settings + tool name + args, then validated behavior by calling set_project/read_recent with explicit context.\\\"}\", \"meta\": {\"component\": \"execution_context\", \"file\": \"server.py\", \"log_type\": \"progress\", \"needed to restore tool operability and root-cause mismatch with client payloads.\\\"}\": \"\", \"preserve sentinel/project tool gating.\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"Scribe MCP calls were failing with missing ExecutionContext\": \"\", \"reasoning\": \"{\\\"how\\\": \\\"Inspected server/tool context flow, edited server.py _call_tool to fill defaults from settings + tool name + args, then validated behavior by calling set_project/read_recent with explicit context.\\\", \\\"what\\\": \\\"Constraints: avoid bypass hacks, keep strict ExecutionContext validation, accept missing client context by normalizing defaults\"}, \"project\": \"scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"raw_line\": \"[\\u26a0\\ufe0f] [2026-01-02 05:38:48 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Audited execution context failures and patched server tool dispatcher to normalize missing context fields (repo_root/mode/intent/affected_dev_projects) before building ExecutionContext; change in server.py to unblock MCP tool calls when client omits context payload. reasoning: {\\\"why\\\":\\\"Scribe MCP calls were failing with missing ExecutionContext; needed to restore tool operability and root-cause mismatch with client payloads.\\\",\\\"what\\\":\\\"Constraints: avoid bypass hacks, keep strict ExecutionContext validation, accept missing client context by normalizing defaults; preserve sentinel/project tool gating.\\\",\\\"how\\\":\\\"Inspected server/tool context flow, edited server.py _call_tool to fill defaults from settings + tool name + args, then validated behavior by calling set_project/read_recent with explicit context.\\\"}   component=execution_context; file=server.py; reasoning={\\\"how\\\": \\\"Inspected server/tool context flow, edited server.py _call_tool to fill defaults from settings + tool name + args, then validated behavior by calling set_project/read_recent with explicit context.\\\", \\\"what\\\": \\\"Constraints: avoid bypass hacks, keep strict ExecutionContext validation, accept missing client context by normalizing defaults; preserve sentinel/project tool gating.\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"Scribe MCP calls were failing with missing ExecutionContext; needed to restore tool operability and root-cause mismatch with client payloads.\\\"}; log_type=progress\", \"ts\": \"2026-01-02 05:38:48 UTC\"}, {\"agent\": \"Codex\", \"emoji\": \"\\u26a0\\ufe0f\", \"message\": \"manage_docs create_doc initially failed due to missing project context; re-established project via set_project and proceeding to retry. reasoning: {\\\"why\\\":\\\"Audit doc required for manage_docs hardening; failure needs traceable recovery.\\\",\\\"what\\\":\\\"Constraints: must use manage_docs; set_project required before doc operations.\\\",\\\"how\\\":\\\"Observed DOC_NOT_FOUND/No project configured error, called set_project, now retrying create_doc.\\\"}\", \"meta\":