{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 05:49:48 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Tool call: read_file | format_requested=readable; response_data={\"chunk\": {\"byte_end\": 4228, \"byte_start\": 2483, \"content\": \"  - `query_entries` can search sentinel logs by time, execution_id, agent identity, intent, dev_project tags, bug/security IDs, and file paths. [Audit D]\\n  - Doc registry keys are canonical, case-insensitive, and aliasable; errors list known doc keys. [Audit E]\\n- **Non-Functional Requirements:**\\n  - Concurrency-safe append semantics for JSON logs; MD remains single-line under lock.\\n  - Deterministic path validation (hard-fail on scope mismatch).\\n- **Assumptions:**\\n  - Repo root is set via `set_project` with absolute path.\\n  - MCP runtime must provide a per-session transport_session_id (or explicit session_id); router hard-fails if missing.\\n- **Risks & Mitigations:**\\n  - **Risk:** Missing session id \\u2192 hard-fail at router; clients must supply transport_session_id or session_id. [Audit B]\\n  - **Risk:** Concurrent append corruption \\u2192 append-only JSONL + file locks; bounded retry. [Audit C]\\n  - **Risk:** Mode confusion \\u2192 router tool gating with clear hard-fail errors. [Audit A,C]\\n  - **Risk:** Mode confusion \\u2192 router tool gating with clear hard-fail errors. [Audit A,C]\\n<!-- ID: architecture_overview -->\\n- **Solution Summary:** Introduce ExecutionContext, session-scoped state, and sentinel logging to make multi-agent work safe and auditable.\\n- **Component Breakdown:**\\n  - **ExecutionContext Validator:** Validates required fields and enforces mode constraints.\\n  - **Session Context Store:** Keeps per-session project/sentinel context (no global leakage).\\n  - **Mode Router:** Exposes only the toolset for the active mode; hard-fails on mismatches.\\n  - **Sentinel Logger:** Writes daily MD + JSONL logs; supports bug/security schemas.\\n  - **read_file Tool:** Reads repo files and logs provenance (sha256, agent identity).\\n\", \"line_end\": 70, \"line_start\": 50}, \"frontmatter\": {\"category\": \"engineering\", \"created_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"doc_type\": \"architecture\", \"id\": \"scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\", \"last_updated\": \"2026-01-03\", \"maintained_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"owners\": [], \"related_docs\": [], \"status\": \"draft\", \"summary\": \"\", \"tags\": [], \"title\": \"\\ud83c\\udfd7\\ufe0f Architecture Guide \\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"version\": \"0.1\"}, \"frontmatter_byte_count\": 338, \"frontmatter_line_count\": 15, \"frontmatter_raw\": \"---\\nid: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\\ntitle: \\\"\\\\U0001F3D7\\\\uFE0F Architecture Guide \\\\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\\\"\\ndoc_type: architecture\\ncategory: engineering\\nstatus: draft\\nversion: '0.1'\\nlast_updated: '2026-01-03'\\nmaintained_by: Corta Labs\\ncreated_by: Corta Labs\\nowners: []\\nrelated_docs: []\\ntags: []\\nsummary: ''\\n---\\n\", \"has_frontmatter\": true, \"mode\": \"line_range\", \"ok\": true, \"reminders\": [{\"category\": \"context\", \"context\": \"Entries:    Last: \", \"emoji\": \"\\ud83c\\udfaf\", \"level\": \"info\", \"message\": \"Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"score\": 3, \"tone\": \"neutral\"}], \"scan\": {\"absolute_path\": \"/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"byte_size\": 10241, \"encoding\": \"utf-8\", \"estimated_chunk_count\": 1, \"line_count\": 157, \"newline_type\": \"LF\", \"repo_relative_path\": \".scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"sha256\": \"3cedbad34d3eedcecac472849647978740c74e8f65435112331fc0d4b4d0d4cd\"}}; timestamp=2026-01-03T05:49:48.629567Z; tool=read_file; priority=medium; log_type=tool_logs; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/TOOL_LOG.jsonl", "id": "2026-01-03T05:49:48.646258+00:00_2a73d8b7", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:49:48.646300+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-03T05:49:48.646258+00:00_2a73d8b7", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:49:48.655926+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 05:50:04 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Tool call: read_file | format_requested=readable; response_data={\"chunk\": {\"byte_end\": 4168, \"byte_start\": 2023, \"content\": \"  - `read_file` logs read provenance in sentinel mode (JSONL required; MD optional). [Audit E]\\n  - Session-scoped context prevents cross-agent leakage; project mode uses ordered resolution. [Audit A]\\n  - `current_project` remains for project mode fallback only; forbidden in sentinel mode with hard error. [Audit A]\\n  - Agents can re-connect to old projects via fingerprint (agent_identity + session_id + repo_root), session-scoped lookup preferred. [Audit B]\\n  - `query_entries` can search sentinel logs by time, execution_id, agent identity, intent, dev_project tags, bug/security IDs, and file paths. [Audit D]\\n- **Non-Functional Requirements:**\\n  - Concurrency-safe append semantics for JSON logs; MD remains single-line under lock.\\n  - Deterministic path validation (hard-fail on scope mismatch).\\n  - Backwards-compatible project-mode behavior.\\n- **Assumptions:**\\n  - Repo root is set via `set_project` with absolute path.\\n  - MCP runtime must provide a per-session transport_session_id (or explicit session_id); router hard-fails if missing.\\n- **Risks & Mitigations:**\\n  - **Risk:** Missing session id \\u2192 hard-fail at router; clients must supply transport_session_id or session_id. [Audit B]\\n  - **Risk:** Concurrent append corruption \\u2192 append-only JSONL + file locks; bounded retry. [Audit C]\\n  - **Risk:** Mode confusion \\u2192 router tool gating with clear hard-fail errors. [Audit A,C]\\n  - **Risk:** Mode confusion \\u2192 router tool gating with clear hard-fail errors. [Audit A,C]\\n<!-- ID: architecture_overview -->\\n- **Solution Summary:** Introduce ExecutionContext, session-scoped state, and sentinel logging to make multi-agent work safe and auditable.\\n- **Component Breakdown:**\\n  - **ExecutionContext Validator:** Validates required fields and enforces mode constraints.\\n  - **Session Context Store:** Keeps per-session project/sentinel context (no global leakage).\\n  - **Mode Router:** Exposes only the toolset for the active mode; hard-fails on mismatches.\\n  - **Sentinel Logger:** Writes daily MD + JSONL logs; supports bug/security schemas.\\n  - **read_file Tool:** Reads repo files and logs provenance (sha256, agent identity).\\n\", \"line_end\": 70, \"line_start\": 46}, \"frontmatter\": {\"category\": \"engineering\", \"created_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"doc_type\": \"architecture\", \"id\": \"scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\", \"last_updated\": \"2026-01-03\", \"maintained_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"owners\": [], \"related_docs\": [], \"status\": \"draft\", \"summary\": \"\", \"tags\": [], \"title\": \"\\ud83c\\udfd7\\ufe0f Architecture Guide \\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"version\": \"0.1\"}, \"frontmatter_byte_count\": 338, \"frontmatter_line_count\": 15, \"frontmatter_raw\": \"---\\nid: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\\ntitle: \\\"\\\\U0001F3D7\\\\uFE0F Architecture Guide \\\\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\\\"\\ndoc_type: architecture\\ncategory: engineering\\nstatus: draft\\nversion: '0.1'\\nlast_updated: '2026-01-03'\\nmaintained_by: Corta Labs\\ncreated_by: Corta Labs\\nowners: []\\nrelated_docs: []\\ntags: []\\nsummary: ''\\n---\\n\", \"has_frontmatter\": true, \"mode\": \"line_range\", \"ok\": true, \"reminders\": [{\"category\": \"context\", \"context\": \"Entries:    Last: \", \"emoji\": \"\\ud83c\\udfaf\", \"level\": \"info\", \"message\": \"Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"score\": 3, \"tone\": \"neutral\"}], \"scan\": {\"absolute_path\": \"/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"byte_size\": 10181, \"encoding\": \"utf-8\", \"estimated_chunk_count\": 1, \"line_count\": 157, \"newline_type\": \"LF\", \"repo_relative_path\": \".scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"sha256\": \"4904c8f458f09cc22aeea820c62bccce257593e6e101aae504523597fa3db0cf\"}}; timestamp=2026-01-03T05:50:04.887487Z; tool=read_file; priority=medium; log_type=tool_logs; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/TOOL_LOG.jsonl", "id": "2026-01-03T05:50:04.904543+00:00_feded17f", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:50:04.904586+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-03T05:50:04.904543+00:00_feded17f", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:50:04.915555+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 05:50:15 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Tool call: read_file | format_requested=readable; response_data={\"chunk\": {\"byte_end\": 5007, \"byte_start\": 3902, \"content\": \"  - **Mode Router:** Exposes only the toolset for the active mode; hard-fails on mismatches.\\n  - **Sentinel Logger:** Writes daily MD + JSONL logs; supports bug/security schemas.\\n  - **read_file Tool:** Reads repo files and logs provenance (sha256, agent identity).\\n  - **query_entries Extension:** Adds sentinel log search by time/filters.\\n- **Data Flow:** MCP call \\u2192 context validation \\u2192 mode router \\u2192 tool execution \\u2192 log append.\\n  - MCP runtime must provide a per-session transport_session_id (or explicit session_id); router hard-fails if missing.\\n- **Risks & Mitigations:**\\n  - **Risk:** Missing session id \\u2192 hard-fail at router; clients must supply transport_session_id or session_id. [Audit B]\\n  - Router validates required fields and injects derived fields before any tool logic. [Audit B]\\n  - Hard-fail if missing/invalid; no silent fallback. [Audit B]\\n- **Session Identity Source (Final)**\\n  - Router generates UUIDv4 session_id per connection and owns it. [Audit B]\\n  - MCP transport identity may be recorded as transport_session_id only; never replaces router session_id. [Audit B]\\n\", \"line_end\": 80, \"line_start\": 68}, \"frontmatter\": {\"category\": \"engineering\", \"created_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"doc_type\": \"architecture\", \"id\": \"scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\", \"last_updated\": \"2026-01-03\", \"maintained_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"owners\": [], \"related_docs\": [], \"status\": \"draft\", \"summary\": \"\", \"tags\": [], \"title\": \"\\ud83c\\udfd7\\ufe0f Architecture Guide \\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"version\": \"0.1\"}, \"frontmatter_byte_count\": 338, \"frontmatter_line_count\": 15, \"frontmatter_raw\": \"---\\nid: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\\ntitle: \\\"\\\\U0001F3D7\\\\uFE0F Architecture Guide \\\\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\\\"\\ndoc_type: architecture\\ncategory: engineering\\nstatus: draft\\nversion: '0.1'\\nlast_updated: '2026-01-03'\\nmaintained_by: Corta Labs\\ncreated_by: Corta Labs\\nowners: []\\nrelated_docs: []\\ntags: []\\nsummary: ''\\n---\\n\", \"has_frontmatter\": true, \"mode\": \"line_range\", \"ok\": true, \"reminders\": [{\"category\": \"context\", \"context\": \"Entries:    Last: \", \"emoji\": \"\\ud83c\\udfaf\", \"level\": \"info\", \"message\": \"Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"score\": 3, \"tone\": \"neutral\"}], \"scan\": {\"absolute_path\": \"/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"byte_size\": 10181, \"encoding\": \"utf-8\", \"estimated_chunk_count\": 1, \"line_count\": 157, \"newline_type\": \"LF\", \"repo_relative_path\": \".scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"sha256\": \"4904c8f458f09cc22aeea820c62bccce257593e6e101aae504523597fa3db0cf\"}}; timestamp=2026-01-03T05:50:14.985738Z; tool=read_file; priority=medium; log_type=tool_logs; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/TOOL_LOG.jsonl", "id": "2026-01-03T05:50:15.002526+00:00_7c694ad6", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:50:15.002566+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-03T05:50:15.002526+00:00_7c694ad6", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:50:15.012764+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 05:50:35 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Tool call: read_file | format_requested=readable; response_data={\"chunk\": {\"byte_end\": 3010, \"byte_start\": 1433, \"content\": \"<!-- ID: requirements_constraints -->\\n- **Functional Requirements:**\\n  - ExecutionContext required on every tool call at router boundary (repo_root, mode, execution_id, agent_identity, intent, timestamp_utc, affected_dev_projects; sentinel_day derived in sentinel mode). [Audit A,B]\\n  - Missing/invalid ExecutionContext = hard-fail with explicit error response. [Audit B]\\n  - Execution/session identity has a single authoritative source at router boundary; no fallback to global state. [Audit B]\\n  - Sentinel logging writes only under `.scribe/sentinel/YYYY-MM-DD/` (MD + JSONL). [Audit C]\\n  - `read_file` logs read provenance in sentinel mode (JSONL required; MD optional). [Audit E]\\n  - Session-scoped context prevents cross-agent leakage; project mode uses ordered resolution. [Audit A]\\n  - `current_project` remains for project mode fallback only; forbidden in sentinel mode with hard error. [Audit A]\\n  - `query_entries` can search sentinel logs by time, execution_id, agent identity, intent, dev_project tags, bug/security IDs, and file paths. [Audit D]\\n  - Doc registry keys are canonical, case-insensitive, and aliasable; errors list known doc keys. [Audit E]\\n  - `query_entries` can search sentinel logs by time, execution_id, agent identity, intent, dev_project tags, bug/security IDs, and file paths. [Audit D]\\n- **Non-Functional Requirements:**\\n  - Concurrency-safe append semantics for JSON logs; MD remains single-line under lock.\\n  - Deterministic path validation (hard-fail on scope mismatch).\\n  - Backwards-compatible project-mode behavior.\\n- **Assumptions:**\\n\", \"line_end\": 56, \"line_start\": 40}, \"frontmatter\": {\"category\": \"engineering\", \"created_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"doc_type\": \"architecture\", \"id\": \"scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\", \"last_updated\": \"2026-01-03\", \"maintained_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"owners\": [], \"related_docs\": [], \"status\": \"draft\", \"summary\": \"\", \"tags\": [], \"title\": \"\\ud83c\\udfd7\\ufe0f Architecture Guide \\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"version\": \"0.1\"}, \"frontmatter_byte_count\": 338, \"frontmatter_line_count\": 15, \"frontmatter_raw\": \"---\\nid: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\\ntitle: \\\"\\\\U0001F3D7\\\\uFE0F Architecture Guide \\\\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\\\"\\ndoc_type: architecture\\ncategory: engineering\\nstatus: draft\\nversion: '0.1'\\nlast_updated: '2026-01-03'\\nmaintained_by: Corta Labs\\ncreated_by: Corta Labs\\nowners: []\\nrelated_docs: []\\ntags: []\\nsummary: ''\\n---\\n\", \"has_frontmatter\": true, \"mode\": \"line_range\", \"ok\": true, \"reminders\": [{\"category\": \"context\", \"context\": \"Entries:    Last: \", \"emoji\": \"\\ud83c\\udfaf\", \"level\": \"info\", \"message\": \"Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"score\": 3, \"tone\": \"neutral\"}], \"scan\": {\"absolute_path\": \"/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"byte_size\": 10299, \"encoding\": \"utf-8\", \"estimated_chunk_count\": 1, \"line_count\": 158, \"newline_type\": \"LF\", \"repo_relative_path\": \".scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"sha256\": \"57ba6bb451317fb8358fae324c4ff4bde0dfcd2992d1dbccaf2dfd8f40c98f16\"}}; timestamp=2026-01-03T05:50:35.701534Z; tool=read_file; priority=medium; log_type=tool_logs; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/TOOL_LOG.jsonl", "id": "2026-01-03T05:50:35.718792+00:00_3953f83f", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:50:35.718839+00:00"}
