{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 05:51:05 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Tool call: read_file | format_requested=readable; response_data={\"chunk\": {\"byte_end\": 3030, \"byte_start\": 1433, \"content\": \"<!-- ID: requirements_constraints -->\\n- **Functional Requirements:**\\n  - ExecutionContext required on every tool call at router boundary (repo_root, mode, execution_id, agent_identity, intent, timestamp_utc, affected_dev_projects; sentinel_day derived in sentinel mode). [Audit A,B]\\n  - Missing/invalid ExecutionContext = hard-fail with explicit error response. [Audit B]\\n  - Sentinel logging writes only under `.scribe/sentinel/YYYY-MM-DD/` (MD + JSONL). [Audit C]\\n  - `read_file` logs read provenance in sentinel mode (JSONL required; MD optional). [Audit E]\\n  - Session-scoped context prevents cross-agent leakage; project mode uses ordered resolution. [Audit A]\\n  - `current_project` remains for project mode fallback only; forbidden in sentinel mode with hard error. [Audit A]\\n  - Agents can re-connect to old projects via fingerprint (agent_identity + session_id + repo_root), session-scoped lookup preferred. [Audit B]\\n  - `query_entries` can search sentinel logs by time, execution_id, agent identity, intent, dev_project tags, bug/security IDs, and file paths. [Audit D]\\n  - Doc registry keys are canonical, case-insensitive, and aliasable; errors list known doc keys. [Audit E]\\n  - `query_entries` can search sentinel logs by time, execution_id, agent identity, intent, dev_project tags, bug/security IDs, and file paths. [Audit D]\\n- **Non-Functional Requirements:**\\n  - Concurrency-safe append semantics for JSON logs; MD remains single-line under lock.\\n  - Deterministic path validation (hard-fail on scope mismatch).\\n  - Backwards-compatible project-mode behavior.\\n- **Assumptions:**\\n\", \"line_end\": 56, \"line_start\": 40}, \"frontmatter\": {\"category\": \"engineering\", \"created_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"doc_type\": \"architecture\", \"id\": \"scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\", \"last_updated\": \"2026-01-03\", \"maintained_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"owners\": [], \"related_docs\": [], \"status\": \"draft\", \"summary\": \"\", \"tags\": [], \"title\": \"\\ud83c\\udfd7\\ufe0f Architecture Guide \\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"version\": \"0.1\"}, \"frontmatter_byte_count\": 338, \"frontmatter_line_count\": 15, \"frontmatter_raw\": \"---\\nid: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\\ntitle: \\\"\\\\U0001F3D7\\\\uFE0F Architecture Guide \\\\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\\\"\\ndoc_type: architecture\\ncategory: engineering\\nstatus: draft\\nversion: '0.1'\\nlast_updated: '2026-01-03'\\nmaintained_by: Corta Labs\\ncreated_by: Corta Labs\\nowners: []\\nrelated_docs: []\\ntags: []\\nsummary: ''\\n---\\n\", \"has_frontmatter\": true, \"mode\": \"line_range\", \"ok\": true, \"reminders\": [{\"category\": \"context\", \"context\": \"Entries:    Last: \", \"emoji\": \"\\ud83c\\udfaf\", \"level\": \"info\", \"message\": \"Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"score\": 3, \"tone\": \"neutral\"}], \"scan\": {\"absolute_path\": \"/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"byte_size\": 10319, \"encoding\": \"utf-8\", \"estimated_chunk_count\": 1, \"line_count\": 158, \"newline_type\": \"LF\", \"repo_relative_path\": \".scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"sha256\": \"ad18048d7455f3c5a7cef86f192ea14b593055e7845c614dbc610c751c2f9cb2\"}}; timestamp=2026-01-03T05:51:05.040266Z; tool=read_file; priority=medium; log_type=tool_logs; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/TOOL_LOG.jsonl", "id": "2026-01-03T05:51:05.057911+00:00_d6b8fd14", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:51:05.057957+00:00"}
