{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 05:51:26 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Tool call: read_file | format_requested=readable; response_data={\"chunk\": {\"byte_end\": 3437, \"byte_start\": 1244, \"content\": \"  - Required tests pass (mode gating, path enforcement, session isolation, read logging, append safety).\\n  - Audit report cites current state with file/line evidence before implementation.\\n<!-- ID: requirements_constraints -->\\n  - ExecutionContext required on every tool call at router boundary (repo_root, mode, execution_id, agent_identity, intent, timestamp_utc, affected_dev_projects; sentinel_day derived in sentinel mode). [Audit A,B]\\n  - Missing/invalid ExecutionContext = hard-fail with explicit error response. [Audit B]\\n  - Execution/session identity has a single authoritative source at router boundary; no fallback to global state. [Audit B]\\n  - Sentinel logging writes only under `.scribe/sentinel/YYYY-MM-DD/` (MD + JSONL). [Audit C]\\n  - `read_file` logs read provenance in sentinel mode (JSONL required; MD optional). [Audit E]\\n  - Session-scoped context prevents cross-agent leakage; project mode uses ordered resolution. [Audit A]\\n  - `current_project` remains for project mode fallback only; forbidden in sentinel mode with hard error. [Audit A]\\n  - Agents can re-connect to old projects via fingerprint (agent_identity + session_id + repo_root), session-scoped lookup preferred. [Audit B]\\n  - `query_entries` can search sentinel logs by time, execution_id, agent identity, intent, dev_project tags, bug/security IDs, and file paths. [Audit D]\\n  - Doc registry keys are canonical, case-insensitive, and aliasable; errors list known doc keys. [Audit E]\\n  - Doc registry keys are canonical, case-insensitive, and aliasable; errors list known doc keys. [Audit E]\\n  - `query_entries` can search sentinel logs by time, execution_id, agent identity, intent, dev_project tags, bug/security IDs, and file paths. [Audit D]\\n- **Non-Functional Requirements:**\\n  - Concurrency-safe append semantics for JSON logs; MD remains single-line under lock.\\n  - Deterministic path validation (hard-fail on scope mismatch).\\n  - Backwards-compatible project-mode behavior.\\n- **Assumptions:**\\n  - Repo root is set via `set_project` with absolute path.\\n  - MCP runtime must provide a per-session transport_session_id (or explicit session_id); router hard-fails if missing.\\n- **Risks & Mitigations:**\\n\", \"line_end\": 60, \"line_start\": 38}, \"frontmatter\": {\"category\": \"engineering\", \"created_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"doc_type\": \"architecture\", \"id\": \"scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\", \"last_updated\": \"2026-01-03\", \"maintained_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"owners\": [], \"related_docs\": [], \"status\": \"draft\", \"summary\": \"\", \"tags\": [], \"title\": \"\\ud83c\\udfd7\\ufe0f Architecture Guide \\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"version\": \"0.1\"}, \"frontmatter_byte_count\": 338, \"frontmatter_line_count\": 15, \"frontmatter_raw\": \"---\\nid: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\\ntitle: \\\"\\\\U0001F3D7\\\\uFE0F Architecture Guide \\\\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\\\"\\ndoc_type: architecture\\ncategory: engineering\\nstatus: draft\\nversion: '0.1'\\nlast_updated: '2026-01-03'\\nmaintained_by: Corta Labs\\ncreated_by: Corta Labs\\nowners: []\\nrelated_docs: []\\ntags: []\\nsummary: ''\\n---\\n\", \"has_frontmatter\": true, \"mode\": \"line_range\", \"ok\": true, \"reminders\": [{\"category\": \"context\", \"context\": \"Entries:    Last: \", \"emoji\": \"\\ud83c\\udfaf\", \"level\": \"info\", \"message\": \"Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"score\": 3, \"tone\": \"neutral\"}], \"scan\": {\"absolute_path\": \"/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"byte_size\": 10520, \"encoding\": \"utf-8\", \"estimated_chunk_count\": 1, \"line_count\": 159, \"newline_type\": \"LF\", \"repo_relative_path\": \".scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"sha256\": \"099bc57bda3795358afae0f92206502fdefffc84b6cc993080b2eade90fe0e2d\"}}; timestamp=2026-01-03T05:51:26.593386Z; tool=read_file; priority=medium; log_type=tool_logs; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/TOOL_LOG.jsonl", "id": "2026-01-03T05:51:26.611235+00:00_a81c8760", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:51:26.611280+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-03T05:51:26.611235+00:00_a81c8760", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:51:26.622632+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 05:51:44 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Tool call: read_file | format_requested=readable; response_data={\"chunk\": {\"byte_end\": 1418, \"byte_start\": 403, \"content\": \"**Author:** Scribe\\n**Version:** Draft v0.1\\n**Status:** Draft\\n**Last Updated:** 2026-01-02 04:17:01 UTC\\n\\n> Architecture guide for scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1.\\n\\n---\\n## 1. Problem Statement\\n<!-- ID: problem_statement -->\\n- **Context:** Implement repo-bound Sentinel Mode with concurrency-safe session isolation and audited reads in the Scribe MCP server.\\n- **Goals:**\\n  - Enforce mode exclusivity (sentinel vs project) with hard-fail gating.\\n  - Provide daily, repo-bound sentinel logs (MD + append-safe JSONL).\\n  - Add a `read_file` tool that logs read provenance (path + sha256 + agent identity).\\n  - Prevent cross-project context leakage under concurrent sessions.\\n- **Non-Goals:**\\n  - Sentinel writes into dev_plan project docs (tags only in Phase 1\\u20132).\\n  - Full write-audit or auto-commit workflows (deferred).\\n- **Success Metrics:**\\n  - Required tests pass (mode gating, path enforcement, session isolation, read logging, append safety).\\n<!-- ID: requirements_constraints -->\\n- **Functional Requirements:**\\n\", \"line_end\": 40, \"line_start\": 18}, \"frontmatter\": {\"category\": \"engineering\", \"created_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"doc_type\": \"architecture\", \"id\": \"scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\", \"last_updated\": \"2026-01-03\", \"maintained_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"owners\": [], \"related_docs\": [], \"status\": \"draft\", \"summary\": \"\", \"tags\": [], \"title\": \"\\ud83c\\udfd7\\ufe0f Architecture Guide \\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"version\": \"0.1\"}, \"frontmatter_byte_count\": 338, \"frontmatter_line_count\": 15, \"frontmatter_raw\": \"---\\nid: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\\ntitle: \\\"\\\\U0001F3D7\\\\uFE0F Architecture Guide \\\\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\\\"\\ndoc_type: architecture\\ncategory: engineering\\nstatus: draft\\nversion: '0.1'\\nlast_updated: '2026-01-03'\\nmaintained_by: Corta Labs\\ncreated_by: Corta Labs\\nowners: []\\nrelated_docs: []\\ntags: []\\nsummary: ''\\n---\\n\", \"has_frontmatter\": true, \"mode\": \"line_range\", \"ok\": true, \"reminders\": [{\"category\": \"context\", \"context\": \"Entries:    Last: \", \"emoji\": \"\\ud83c\\udfaf\", \"level\": \"info\", \"message\": \"Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"score\": 3, \"tone\": \"neutral\"}], \"scan\": {\"absolute_path\": \"/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"byte_size\": 10359, \"encoding\": \"utf-8\", \"estimated_chunk_count\": 1, \"line_count\": 158, \"newline_type\": \"LF\", \"repo_relative_path\": \".scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"sha256\": \"9b031eb969877c4c269754fc4edf1477c506d660f0f6456623f0791df16905b4\"}}; timestamp=2026-01-03T05:51:44.446173Z; tool=read_file; priority=medium; log_type=tool_logs; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/TOOL_LOG.jsonl", "id": "2026-01-03T05:51:44.463036+00:00_ca1a3ef7", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:51:44.463078+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-03T05:51:44.463036+00:00_ca1a3ef7", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:51:44.473960+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 05:51:50 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Tool call: read_file | format_requested=readable; response_data={\"chunk\": {\"byte_end\": 3725, \"byte_start\": 1071, \"content\": \"- **Non-Goals:**\\n  - Sentinel writes into dev_plan project docs (tags only in Phase 1\\u20132).\\n  - Full write-audit or auto-commit workflows (deferred).\\n- **Success Metrics:**\\n  - Required tests pass (mode gating, path enforcement, session isolation, read logging, append safety).\\n<!-- ID: requirements_constraints -->\\n- **Functional Requirements:**\\n  - ExecutionContext required on every tool call at router boundary (repo_root, mode, execution_id, agent_identity, intent, timestamp_utc, affected_dev_projects; sentinel_day derived in sentinel mode). [Audit A,B]\\n  - Missing/invalid ExecutionContext = hard-fail with explicit error response. [Audit B]\\n  - Execution/session identity has a single authoritative source at router boundary; no fallback to global state. [Audit B]\\n  - Sentinel logging writes only under `.scribe/sentinel/YYYY-MM-DD/` (MD + JSONL). [Audit C]\\n  - `read_file` logs read provenance in sentinel mode (JSONL required; MD optional). [Audit E]\\n  - Session-scoped context prevents cross-agent leakage; project mode uses ordered resolution. [Audit A]\\n  - `current_project` remains for project mode fallback only; forbidden in sentinel mode with hard error. [Audit A]\\n  - Agents can re-connect to old projects via fingerprint (agent_identity + session_id + repo_root), session-scoped lookup preferred. [Audit B]\\n  - `query_entries` can search sentinel logs by time, execution_id, agent identity, intent, dev_project tags, bug/security IDs, and file paths. [Audit D]\\n  - Doc registry keys are canonical, case-insensitive, and aliasable; errors list known doc keys. [Audit E]\\n  - `query_entries` can search sentinel logs by time, execution_id, agent identity, intent, dev_project tags, bug/security IDs, and file paths. [Audit D]\\n- **Non-Functional Requirements:**\\n  - Concurrency-safe append semantics for JSON logs; MD remains single-line under lock.\\n  - Deterministic path validation (hard-fail on scope mismatch).\\n  - Backwards-compatible project-mode behavior.\\n- **Assumptions:**\\n  - Repo root is set via `set_project` with absolute path.\\n  - MCP runtime must provide a per-session transport_session_id (or explicit session_id); router hard-fails if missing.\\n- **Risks & Mitigations:**\\n  - **Risk:** Missing session id \\u2192 hard-fail at router; clients must supply transport_session_id or session_id. [Audit B]\\n  - **Risk:** Concurrent append corruption \\u2192 append-only JSONL + file locks; bounded retry. [Audit C]\\n  - **Risk:** Mode confusion \\u2192 router tool gating with clear hard-fail errors. [Audit A,C]\\n  - **Risk:** Mode confusion \\u2192 router tool gating with clear hard-fail errors. [Audit A,C]\\n<!-- ID: architecture_overview -->\\n\", \"line_end\": 64, \"line_start\": 34}, \"frontmatter\": {\"category\": \"engineering\", \"created_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"doc_type\": \"architecture\", \"id\": \"scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\", \"last_updated\": \"2026-01-03\", \"maintained_by\": \"Corta Labs\", \"owners\": [], \"related_docs\": [], \"status\": \"draft\", \"summary\": \"\", \"tags\": [], \"title\": \"\\ud83c\\udfd7\\ufe0f Architecture Guide \\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"version\": \"0.1\"}, \"frontmatter_byte_count\": 338, \"frontmatter_line_count\": 15, \"frontmatter_raw\": \"---\\nid: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1-architecture\\ntitle: \\\"\\\\U0001F3D7\\\\uFE0F Architecture Guide \\\\u2014 scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\\\"\\ndoc_type: architecture\\ncategory: engineering\\nstatus: draft\\nversion: '0.1'\\nlast_updated: '2026-01-03'\\nmaintained_by: Corta Labs\\ncreated_by: Corta Labs\\nowners: []\\nrelated_docs: []\\ntags: []\\nsummary: ''\\n---\\n\", \"has_frontmatter\": true, \"mode\": \"line_range\", \"ok\": true, \"reminders\": [{\"category\": \"context\", \"context\": \"Entries:    Last: \", \"emoji\": \"\\ud83c\\udfaf\", \"level\": \"info\", \"message\": \"Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1\", \"score\": 3, \"tone\": \"neutral\"}], \"scan\": {\"absolute_path\": \"/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"byte_size\": 10359, \"encoding\": \"utf-8\", \"estimated_chunk_count\": 1, \"line_count\": 158, \"newline_type\": \"LF\", \"repo_relative_path\": \".scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"sha256\": \"9b031eb969877c4c269754fc4edf1477c506d660f0f6456623f0791df16905b4\"}}; timestamp=2026-01-03T05:51:50.083478Z; tool=read_file; priority=medium; log_type=tool_logs; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1/TOOL_LOG.jsonl", "id": "2026-01-03T05:51:50.100890+00:00_9ba76958", "timestamp": "2026-01-03T05:51:50.100933+00:00"}
