ext in calls.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}, \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"raw_line\\\": \\\"[\\\\u2705] [2026-01-03 06:07:53 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Adjusted read_file to allow usage without a session-scoped project and added server-side transport_session_id fallback from MCP kwargs (session_id/client_id/connection_id) to auto-supply context when available; still hard-fails if no transport/session id.   reasoning={\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Set resolve_logging_context(require_project=False) in read_file logging and added kwargs-based transport_session_id fallback in server call_tool before enforcing session identity.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: keep session identity requirement for concurrency; avoid reintroducing global project fallback; only relax read_file project requirement.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"User requested auto-supplied context and global read_file access without set_project; current enforcement blocked read_file and forced manual context in calls.\\\\\\\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\\", \\\"ts\\\": \\\"2026-01-03 06:07:53 UTC\\\"}, {\\\"agent\\\": \\\"Codex\\\", \\\"category\\\": null, \\\"confidence\\\": 1.0, \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"\\\\u2705\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"fee87dc4490d5c79426f70b5b56d1b6d\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aligned set_project session_projects mapping with router ExecutionContext by using context.session_id (when available) for state_manager.set_current_project; preserves agent_manager session id for DB while unblocking session-scoped project resolution.\\\", \\\"meta\\\": {\\\"content_type\\\": \\\"log\\\", \\\"log_type\\\": \\\"progress\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Captured ExecutionContext in set_project and passed context.session_id to state_manager.set_current_project (fallback to agent session id if absent).\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: keep agent_manager session id for DB/audit; avoid breaking legacy fallback; use ExecutionContext when present.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Read_file/logging now resolve session projects by exec_context.session_id; using only agent_manager session id left session_projects empty for tool calls tied to transport_session_id.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}, \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"raw_line\\\": \\\"[\\\\u2705] [2026-01-03 06:04:34 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Aligned set_project session_projects mapping with router ExecutionContext by using context.session_id (when available) for state_manager.set_current_project; preserves agent_manager session id for DB while unblocking session-scoped project resolution.   reasoning={\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Captured ExecutionContext in set_project and passed context.session_id to state_manager.set_current_project (fallback to agent session id if absent).\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: keep agent_manager session id for DB/audit; avoid breaking legacy fallback; use ExecutionContext when present.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Read_file/logging now resolve session projects by exec_context.session_id; using only agent_manager session id left session_projects empty for tool calls tied to transport_session_id.\\\\\\\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\\", \\\"ts\\\": \\\"2026-01-03 06:04:34 UTC\\\"}, {\\\"agent\\\": \\\"Codex\\\", \\\"category\\\": null, \\\"confidence\\\": 1.0, \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"\\\\u26a0\\\\ufe0f\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"58b4fa2f0b4adc41f05710a56b373042\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"read_file failed before session context was bound: \\\\\\\"No session-scoped project configured\\\\\\\"; set_project re-run with transport_session_id to bind context before further inspection.\\\", \\\"meta\\\": {\\\"content_type\\\": \\\"log\\\", \\\"log_type\\\": \\\"progress\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Re-ran set_project with transport_session_id=codex-session-verify, then proceeded to re-attempt read_file.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: must log tool failures; need to set_project with same session id before further tool calls; keep context consistent.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Step 2 blocks project-mode global fallback, so read_file requires a session-scoped project; initial attempt lacked that binding.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}, \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"raw_line\\\": \\\"[\\\\u26a0\\\\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 06:03:50 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] read_file failed before session context was bound: \\\\\\\"No session-scoped project configured\\\\\\\"; set_project re-run with transport_session_id to bind context before further inspection.   reasoning={\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Re-ran set_project with transport_session_id=codex-session-verify, then proceeded to re-attempt read_file.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: must log tool failures; need to set_project with same session id before further tool calls; keep context consistent.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Step 2 blocks project-mode global fallback, so read_file requires a session-scoped project; initial attempt lacked that binding.\\\\\\\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\\", \\\"ts\\\": \\\"2026-01-03 06:03:50 UTC\\\"}, {\\\"agent\\\": \\\"Codex\\\", \\\"category\\\": null, \\\"confidence\\\": 1.0, \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"\\\\u2705\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"ebb9e3d37a188e99551440a280507f7e\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Step 3 concurrency fix: added mirror_global flag to StateManager.set_current_project, stopped set_project from updating global current_project when agent session succeeds, and prevented manage_docs registry updates from mutating global current_project; added state manager test for session-only updates.\\\", \\\"meta\\\": {\\\"content_type\\\": \\\"log\\\", \\\"log_type\\\": \\\"progress\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Updated state/manager.py to support mirror_global, set tools/set_project.py to disable global mirroring when agent context succeeds, set tools/manage_docs.py registry updates to mirror_global=False, and added tests/test_utils.py coverage for session-only updates.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: keep legacy fallback for non-session flows; avoid touching unrelated callers; add minimal test coverage.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Step 3 requires removing global current_project mirroring so concurrent sessions don't overwrite each other while preserving legacy behavior when no session context exists.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}, \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"raw_line\\\": \\\"[\\\\u2705] [2026-01-03 05:59:08 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Step 3 concurrency fix: added mirror_global flag to StateManager.set_current_project, stopped set_project from updating global current_project when agent session succeeds, and prevented manage_docs registry updates from mutating global current_project; added state manager test for session-only updates.   reasoning={\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Updated state/manager.py to support mirror_global, set tools/set_project.py to disable global mirroring when agent context succeeds, set tools/manage_docs.py registry updates to mirror_global=False, and added tests/test_utils.py coverage for session-only updates.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: keep legacy fallback for non-session flows; avoid touching unrelated callers; add minimal test coverage.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Step 3 requires removing global current_project mirroring so concurrent sessions don't overwrite each other while preserving legacy behavior when no session context exists.\\\\\\\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\\", \\\"ts\\\": \\\"2026-01-03 05:59:08 UTC\\\"}, {\\\"agent\\\": \\\"Scribe\\\", \\\"category\\\": null, \\\"confidence\\\": 1.0, \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"\\\\u2139\\\\ufe0f\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1dbc4169a1aa4b1b60fc703a1a45e5a2\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Tool call: read_file\\\", \\\"meta\\\": {\\\"content_type\\\": \\\"log\\\", \\\"format_requested\\\": \\\"readable\\\", \\\"log_type\\\": \\\"tool_logs\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"response_data\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"chunks\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"byte_end\\\\\\\": 3369, \\\\\\\"byte_start\\\\\\\": 0, \\\\\\\"chunk_index\\\\\\\": 0, \\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Unit tests for utility helpers and state management.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nimport json\\\\\\\\nimport shutil\\\\\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nimport pytest\\\\\\\\nimport sys\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Add the MCP_SPINE directory to Python path for imports\\\\\\\\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).parent.parent))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nfrom scribe_mcp.state.manager import StateManager\\\\\\\\nfrom scribe_mcp.config.settings import settings\\\\\\\\nfrom scribe_mcp.tools import set_project\\\\\\\\nfrom scribe_mcp.tools.append_entry import (\\\\\\\\n    _normalise_meta,\\\\\\\\n    _sanitize_identifier,\\\\\\\\n    _validate_message,\\\\\\\\n)\\\\\\\\nfrom scribe_mcp.shared.logging_utils import _clean_meta_value\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef test_sanitize_identifier_strips_brackets():\\\\\\\\n    assert _sanitize_identifier(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"[Agent: Test]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Agent: Test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    assert _sanitize_identifier(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" Scribe \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Scribe\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    assert _sanitize_identifier(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"   \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Scribe\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef test_validate_message_disallows_newlines_and_pipes():\\\\\\\\n    assert _validate_message(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nworld\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Message cannot contain newline characters.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    assert _validate_message(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"pipe   value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Message cannot contain pipe characters.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    assert _validate_message(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"valid message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") is None\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef test_normalise_meta_orders_and_sanitises_keys():\\\\\\\\n    meta = {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"b key\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nline\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 1}\\\\\\\\n    pairs = _normalise_meta(meta)\\\\\\\\n    assert pairs == ((\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"b_key\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"value line\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef test_clean_meta_value_replaces_newlines_and_pipes():\\\\\\\\n    assert _clean_meta_value(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"line1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nline2 x\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"line1 line2 x\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\\\\\\\\nasync def test_set_project_rejects_log_outside_root(tmp_path: Path):\\\\\\\\n    safe_root = tmp_path / \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"safe_root\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    outside_log = tmp_path / \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"elsewhere\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"PROGRESS_LOG.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    result = await set_project.set_project(\\\\\\\\n        name=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"malicious\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        root=str(safe_root),\\\\\\\\n        progress_log=str(outside_log),\\\\\\\\n    )\\\\\\\\n    assert not result[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\n    assert \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Progress log must be within the project root.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" in result[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\\\\\\\\nasync def test_set_project_allows_external_root(tmp_path: Path):\\\\\\\\n    external_root = tmp_path / \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"external