\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Step 3 concurrency fix: added mirror_global flag to StateManager.set_current_project, stopped set_project from updating global current_project when agent session succeeds, and prevented manage_docs registry updates from mutating global current_project; added state manager test for session-only updates.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"meta\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"content_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"log\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"log_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"progress\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"priority\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reasoning\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Updated state/manager.py to support mirror_global, set tools/set_project.py to disable global mirroring when agent context succeeds, set tools/manage_docs.py registry updates to mirror_global=False, and added tests/test_utils.py coverage for session-only updates.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Constraints: keep legacy fallback for non-session flows; avoid touching unrelated callers; add minimal test coverage.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Step 3 requires removing global current_project mirroring so concurrent sessions don't overwrite each other while preserving legacy behavior when no session context exists.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"priority\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"raw_line\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"[\\\\\\\\u2705] [2026-01-03 05:59:08 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Step 3 concurrency fix: added mirror_global flag to StateManager.set_current_project, stopped set_project from updating global current_project when agent session succeeds, and prevented manage_docs registry updates from mutating global current_project; added state manager test for session-only updates.   reasoning={\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Updated state/manager.py to support mirror_global, set tools/set_project.py to disable global mirroring when agent context succeed