1-03 06:32:48 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Tool call: read_recent   format_requested=readable; response_data={\\\"count\\\": 15, \\\"entries\\\": [{\\\"agent\\\": \\\"Codex\\\", \\\"category\\\": null, \\\"confidence\\\": 1.0, \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"\\\\u2139\\\\ufe0f\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"ec9af0d6a666af3c40231a50229e21f0\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Acknowledged shift to default sentinel mode to avoid rejecting logs and keep isolated audits clean; will adjust ExecutionContext default mode and routing rules so tools without set_project route to sentinel logs (global daily).\\\", \\\"meta\\\": {\\\"content_type\\\": \\\"log\\\", \\\"log_type\\\": \\\"progress\\\", \\\"phase\\\": \\\"planning\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"low\\\", \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Plan to set default mode to sentinel when no explicit project context is provided, update tool routing to log to sentinel for missing session project, and keep project tools requiring explicit set_project.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: sentinel logs are global daily; project audits must stay isolated; no silent project auto-select; tools must still enforce sentinel-only restrictions.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"User clarified default should be sentinel mode so missing project context logs still land in global sentinel logs and avoid audit pollution.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}, \\\"priority\\\": \\\"low\\\", \\\"raw_line\\\": \\\"[\\\\u2139\\\\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 06:32:02 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Acknowledged shift to default sentinel mode to avoid rejecting logs and keep isolated audits clean; will adjust ExecutionContext default mode and routing rules so tools without set_project route to sentinel logs (global daily).   phase=planning; reasoning={\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Plan to set default mode to sentinel when no explicit project context is provided, update tool routing to log to sentinel for missing session project, and keep project tools requiring explicit set_project.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: sentinel logs are global daily; project audits must stay isolated; no silent project auto-select; tools must still enforce sentinel-only restrictions.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"User clarified default should be sentinel mode so missing project context logs still land in global sentinel logs and avoid audit pollution.\\\\\\\"}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\\", \\\"ts\\\": \\\"2026-01-03 06:32:02 UTC\\\"}, {\\\"agent\\\": \\\"Codex\\\", \\\"category\\\": null, \\\"confidence\\\": 1.0, \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"\\\\u2139\\\\ufe0f\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"93ad5844e723782813fd1e14b1f120bd\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Outlined options for session/agent registry and project routing to reduce confusion in multi-project concurrency; will propose SQLite-backed session registry and agent-recent routing with guardrails before implementing.\\\", \\\"meta\\\": {\\\"content_type\\\": \\\"log\\\", \\\"log_type\\\": \\\"progress\\\", \\\"phase\\\": \\\"planning\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"low\\\", \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Summarize design options and tradeoffs, propose registry schema + routing rules, and ask for confirmation before coding.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: preserve concurrency, avoid confusing new-project flows, minimize manual parameters, support subagent project auto-selection.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"User asked for thoughts on temporal backing/registry and agent-to-project routing before development.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}, \\\"priority\\\": \\\"low\\\", \\\"raw_line\\\": \\\"[\\\\u2139\\\\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 06:23:35 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Outlined options for session/agent registry and project routing to reduce confusion in multi-project concurrency; will propose SQLite-backed session registry and agent-recent routing with guardrails before implementing.   phase=planning; reasoning={\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Summarize design options and tradeoffs, propose registry schema + routing rules, and ask for confirmation before coding.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: preserve concurrency, avoid confusing new-project flows, minimize manual parameters, support subagent project auto-selection.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"User asked for thoughts on temporal backing/registry and agent-to-project routing before development.\\\\\\\"}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\\", \\\"ts\\\": \\\"2026-01-03 06:23:35 UTC\\\"}, {\\\"agent\\\": \\\"Codex\\\", \\\"category\\\": null, \\\"confidence\\\": 1.0, \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"\\\\u2139\\\\ufe0f\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"56ba5a4c1de5f8398b8fac473e9153f3\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Audited set_project implementation for session/concurrency plumbing (imports, session_id handling, agent_manager fallback, state_manager session_id usage, duplicate ProjectRegistry init).\\\", \\\"meta\\\": {\\\"content_type\\\": \\\"log\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\"[\\\\\\\"tools/set_project.py\\\\\\\"]\\\", \\\"log_type\\\": \\\"progress\\\", \\\"phase\\\": \\\"audit\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"low\\\", \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Scanned tools/set_project.py chunks to locate agent/session handling and state_manager update paths, plus duplicate ProjectRegistry setup.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: use read_file for inspection; avoid full log reads; identify session-context usage and potential improvements.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"User asked for set_project plumbing audit and guidance on multi-session validation.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}, \\\"priority\\\": \\\"low\\\", \\\"raw_line\\\": \\\"[\\\\u2139\\\\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 06:21:06 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Audited set_project implementation for session/concurrency plumbing (imports, session_id handling, agent_manager fallback, state_manager session_id usage, duplicate ProjectRegistry init).   files=[\\\\\\\"tools/set_project.py\\\\\\\"]; phase=audit; reasoning={\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Scanned tools/set_project.py chunks to locate agent/session handling and state_manager update paths, plus duplicate ProjectRegistry setup.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Constraints: use read_file for inspection; avoid full log reads; identify session-context usage and potential improvements.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"User asked for set_project plumbing audit and guidance on multi-session validation.\\\\\\\"}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\\", \\\"ts\\\": \\\"2026-01-03 06:21:06 UTC\\\"}, {\\\"agent\\\": \\\"Scribe\\\", \\\"category\\\": null, \\\"confidence\\\": 1.0, \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"\\\\u2139\\\\ufe0f\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"68d718798a619e7458d420300e8b3133\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Tool call: read_file\\\", \\\"meta\\\": {\\\"content_type\\\": \\\"log\\\", \\\"format_requested\\\": \\\"readable\\\", \\\"log_type\\\": \\\"tool_logs\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"response_data\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"chunks\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"byte_end\\\\\\\": 21599, \\\\\\\"byte_start\\\\\\\": 15468, \\\\\\\"chunk_index\\\\\\\": 2, \\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"async def _ensure_documents(\\\\\\\\n    name: str,\\\\\\\\n    author: Optional[str],\\\\\\\\n    overwrite: bool,\\\\\\\\n    root_path: Path,\\\\\\\\n    docs_dir: Path,\\\\\\\\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    Ensure project documentation exists with proper idempotency.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    This function checks if documentation already exists and skips generation\\\\\\\\n    unless explicitly requested to overwrite, making it truly idempotent.\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    # Check if docs already exist\\\\\\\\n    doc_files = {\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"architecture\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": docs_dir / \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"phase_plan\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": docs_dir / \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"PHASE_PLAN.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"checklist\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": docs_dir / \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CHECKLIST.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"progress_log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": docs_dir / \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"PROGRESS_LOG.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"doc_log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": docs_dir / \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"DOC_LOG.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"security_log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": docs_dir / \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"SECURITY_LOG.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"bug_log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": docs_dir / \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"BUG_LOG.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    existing_files = []\\\\\\\\n    missing_files = []\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    for doc_type, file_path in doc_files.items():\\\\\\\\n        if file_path.exists() and file_path.stat().st_size > 0:\\\\\\\\n            existing_files.append(doc_type)\\\\\\\\n        else:\\\\\\\\n            missing_files.append(doc_type)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    # If all files exist and we're not overwriting, skip generation\\\\\\\\n    if not missing_files and not overwrite:\\\\\\\\n        return {\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": True,\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"generated\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [],\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"skipped\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": list(doc_files.keys()),\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"docs_already_exist\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"All documentation files already exist for project '{name}'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n        }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    # Generate missing files (or all if overwriting)\\\\\\\\n    from scribe_mcp.tools import generate_doc_templates as doc_templates\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    result = await doc_templates.generate_doc_templates(\\\\\\\\n        project_name=name,\\\\\\\\n        author=author,\\\\\\\\n        overwrite=overwrite,\\\\\\\\n        # Thread the resolved docs_dir through to guarantee templates land in the\\\\\\\\n        # same location set_project will return (supports `.scribe` normalization\\\\\\\\n        # and legacy docs/dev_plans back-compat).\\\\\\\\n        base_dir=str(docs_dir),\\\\\\\\n    )\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    # Add detailed status about what was done\\\\\\\\n    if result.get(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"):\\\\\\\\n        result[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"idempotent_status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"] = {\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"existing_files\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": existing_files,\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"missing_files_before\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": missing_files,\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"overwrite_requested\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": overwrite\\\\\\\\n        }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    return result\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nasync def _validate_project_paths(\\\\\\\\n    *,\\\\\\\\n    name: str,\\\\\\\\n    root_path: Path,\\\\\\\\n    docs_dir: Path,\\\\\\\\n    progress_log: Path,\\\\\\\\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Ensure the provided paths do not collide with existing project definitions.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    warnings: List[str] = []\\\\\\\\n    existing = await _gather_known_projects(skip=name)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    root_resolved = root_path.resolve()\\\\\\\\n    docs_resolved = docs_dir.resolve()\\\\\\\\n    log_resolved = progress_log.resolve()\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    for other_name, paths in existing.items():\\\\\\\\n        if paths[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"progress_log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"] == log_resolved:\\\\\\\\n            return {\\\\\\\\n                \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": False,\\\\\\\\n                \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Progress log '{log_resolved}' already belongs to project '{other_name}'.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            }\\\\\\\\n        if paths[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"docs_dir\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"] == docs_resolved:\\\\\\\\n            return {\\\\\\\\n                \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": False,\\\\\\\\n                \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Docs directory '{docs_resolved}' already belongs to project '{other_name}'.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            }\\\\\\\\n    root_parent = _first_existing_parent(root_resolved)\\\\\\\\n    if not os.access(root_parent, os.W_OK):\\\\\\\\n        return {\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": False,\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Insufficient permissions to write under '{root_parent}'.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    docs_parent = _first_existing_parent(docs_resolved)\\\\\\\\n    if not os.access(docs_parent, os.W_OK):\\\\\\\\n        return {\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": False,\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Insufficient permissions to write docs under '{docs_parent}'.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    log_parent = _first_existing_parent(log_resolved.parent)\\\\\\\\n    if not os.access(log_parent, os.W_OK):\\\\\\\\n        return {\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": False,\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Insufficient permissions to write progress log under '{log_parent}'.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    return {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": True, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"warnings\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": warnings}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nasync def _gather_known_projects(skip: Optional[str]) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Path]]:\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Collect registered projects from state and configs.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    collected: Dict[str, Dict[str, Path]] = {}\\\\\\\\n    state = await server_mo