 \\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Progress log is required before work; reboot cleared session context so set_project was needed to bind the session and verify logs.\\\\\\\"}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\\", \\\"ts\\\": \\\"2026-01-03 06:11:36 UTC\\\"}, {\\\"agent\\\": \\\"Scribe\\\", \\\"category\\\": null, \\\"confidence\\\": 1.0, \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"\\\\u2139\\\\ufe0f\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"4caf510e5a4fe9b489c4711fa991c1b5\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Tool call: read_recent\\\", \\\"meta\\\": {\\\"content_type\\\": \\\"log\\\", \\\"format_requested\\\": \\\"readable\\\", \\\"log_type\\\": \\\"tool_logs\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"response_data\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"count\\\\\\\": 10, \\\\\\\"entries\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"agent\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Codex\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": null, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": 1.0, \\\\\\\"emoji\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\u2705\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ed9e3efec3d657af9bd456b55401f17f\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Adjusted read_file to allow usage without a session-scoped project and added server-side transport_session_id fallback from MCP kwargs (session_id/client_id/connection_id) to auto-supply context when available; still hard-fails if no transport/session id.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"meta\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"content_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"log\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"log_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"progress\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"priority\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reasoning\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Set resolve_logging_context(require_project=False) in read_file logging and added kwargs-based transport_session_id fallback in server call_tool before enforcing session identity.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Constraints: keep session identity requirement for concurrency; avoid reintroducing global project fallback; only relax read_file project requirement.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"User requested auto-supplied context and global read_file access without set_project; current enforcement blocked read_file and forced manual context in calls.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"priority\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"raw_line\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"[\\\\\\\\u2705] [2026-01-03 06:07:53 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Adjusted read_file to allow usage without a session-scoped project and added server-side transport_session_id fallback from MCP kwargs (session_id/client_id/connection_id) to auto-supply context when available; still hard-fails if no transport/session id.   reasoning={\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Set resolve_logging_context(require_project=False) in read_file logging and added kwargs-based transport_session_id fallback in server call_tool before enforcing session identity.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Constraints: keep session identity requirement for concurrency; avoid reintroducing global project fallback; only relax read_file project requirement.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"User requested auto-supplied context and global read_file access without set_project; current enforcement blocked read_file and forced manual context in calls.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"ts\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2026-01-03 06:07:53 UTC\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"agent\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Codex\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": null, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": 1.0, \\\\\\\"emoji\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\u2705\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"fee87dc4490d5c79426f70b5b56d1b6d\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Aligned set_project session_projects mapping with router ExecutionContext by using context.session_id (when available) for state_manager.set_current_project; preserves agent_manager session id for DB while unblocking session-scoped project resolution.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"meta\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"content_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"log\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"log_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"progress\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"priority\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reasoning\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Captured ExecutionContext in set_project and passed context.session_id to state_manager.set_current_project (fallback to agent session id if absent).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Constraints: keep agent_manager session id for DB/audit; avoid breaking legacy fallback; use ExecutionContext when present.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Read_file/logging now resolve session projects by exec_context.session_id; using only agent_manager session id left session_projects empty for tool calls tied to transport_session_id.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"priority\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"raw_line\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"[\\\\\\\\u2705] [2026-01-03 06:04:34 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Aligned set_project session_projects mapping with router ExecutionContext by using context.session_id (when available) for state_manager.set_current_project; preserves agent_manager session id for DB while unblocking session-scoped project resolution.   reasoning={\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Captured ExecutionContext in set_project and passed context.session_id to state_manager.set_current_project (fallback to agent session id if absent).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Constraints: keep agent_manager session id for DB/audit; avoid breaking legacy fallback; use ExecutionContext when present.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Read_file/logging now resolve session projects by exec_context.session_id; using only agent_manager session id left session_projects empty for tool calls tied to transport_session_id.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"ts\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2026-01-03 06:04:34 UTC\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"agent\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Codex\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": null, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": 1.0, \\\\\\\"emoji\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\u26a0\\\\\\\\ufe0f\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"58b4fa2f0b4adc41f05710a56b373042\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"read_file failed before session context was bound: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No session-scoped project configured\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; set_project re-run with transport_session_id to bind context before further inspection.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"meta\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"content_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"log\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"log_type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"progress\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"priority\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reasoning\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Re-ran set_project with transport_session_id=codex-session-verify, then proceeded to re-attempt read_file.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Constraints: must log tool failures; need to set_project with same session id before further tool calls; keep context consistent.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"why\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Step 2 blocks project-mode global fallback, so read_file requires a session-scoped project; initial attempt lacked that binding.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"priority\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"raw_line\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"[\\\\\\\\u26a0\\\\\\\\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 06:03:50 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] read_file failed before session context was bound: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No session-scoped project configured\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; set_project re-run with transport_session_id to bind context before further inspection.   reasoning={\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Re-ran set_project with transport_session_id=codex-session-verify, then proceeded to