{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 09:29:52 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Tool call: read_recent | format_requested=readable; response_data={\"count\": 10, \"entries\": [{\"agent\": \"Codex\", \"category\": null, \"confidence\": 1.0, \"emoji\": \"\\u2139\\ufe0f\", \"id\": \"ed2ca562f3e20025251a9a461ecbb2e9\", \"message\": \"Step 2 in progress: added SQLite session registry tables and wired router/set_project/session resolution to DB with JSON fallback for multi-process concurrency.\", \"meta\": {\"content_type\": \"log\", \"files\": \"[\\\"storage/sqlite.py\\\", \\\"server.py\\\", \\\"tools/set_project.py\\\", \\\"shared/logging_utils.py\\\"]\", \"log_type\": \"progress\", \"phase\": \"implementation\", \"priority\": \"low\", \"reasoning\": \"{\\\"how\\\": \\\"Added scribe_sessions/session_projects/agent_recent_projects tables + SQLite methods; router reads session mode from DB; set_project writes session project/mode to DB; logging_utils reads session project from DB when available.\\\", \\\"what\\\": \\\"Constraints: keep JSON state as fallback; avoid breaking non-SQLite backends; maintain sentinel default behavior.\\\", \\\"why\\\": \\\"Step 2 requires DB-backed session/mode/project state so multiple server processes share context.\\\"}\"}, \"priority\": \"low\", \"raw_line\": \"[\\u2139\\ufe0f] [2026-01-03 07:00:15 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: scribe_sentinel_concurrency_v1] Step 2 in progress: added SQLite session registry tables and wired router/set_project/session resolution to DB with JSON fallback for multi-process concurrency.   files=[\\\"storage/sqlite.py\\\", \\\"server.py\\\", \\\"tools/set_project.py\\\", \\\"shared/logging_utils.py\\\"]; phase=implementation; reasoning={\\\"how\\\": \\\"Added scribe_sessions/session_projects/agent_recent_projects tables + SQLite methods; router reads session mode from DB; set_project writes session project/mode to DB; logging_utils reads session project from DB w